---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Prose from '../components/Prose.astro';
import { site } from '../site.config.ts';
---

<Base title="Privacy Policy" description="How Zenith handles your data: what is collected, why, and how to delete it.">
  <Prose title="Privacy Policy" lede="Last updated: September 28, 2026">
    <h2>1. Overview</h2>
    <p>
      Zenith ("we", "our" or "us") provides the Zenith mobile app and the service behind it. We believe in privacy by
      design: <strong>Zenith works fully without an account</strong>. This policy explains what information is
      collected, how it is used and how it is protected.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Information we collect</h2>
    <h3>A. Guest mode (no account)</h3>
    <p>
      If you use Zenith without an account, your library, watch progress and preferences are stored
      <strong>only on your device</strong>. They are never sent to our account database unless you sign up and choose
      to back them up.
    </p>
    <h3>B. Account (optional)</h3>
    <p>If you create an account to sync your library across devices, we store:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Username and email</strong>, used for signing in and account recovery.</li>
      <li>
        <strong>Password</strong>, stored only as a bcrypt hash. We never see or store your password in plain text.
      </li>
      <li><strong>Library and watch history</strong>: the shows, movies, seasons and episodes you track.</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>C. Technical logs</h3>
    <p>
      When the app talks to our servers, basic diagnostic data (such as your IP address, used temporarily for rate
      limiting, and error reports) may be processed to keep the service reliable and prevent abuse.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Third parties and advertising</h2>
    <h3>A. The Movie Database (TMDB)</h3>
    <p>
      Zenith gets public movie and TV information from TMDB. Your personal information, watch history and email are
      never shared with TMDB.
    </p>
    <h3>B. Trakt (optional)</h3>
    <p>
      If you connect your Trakt account, Zenith syncs your watched episodes with your Trakt profile. You can disconnect
      Trakt at any time in Settings.
    </p>
    <h3>C. Google AdMob</h3>
    <p>
      The mobile app shows small banner ads from Google AdMob. Google may use device identifiers (such as the Android
      Advertising ID) to show personalized or non-personalized ads, depending on your consent.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Your choices:</strong> in the EEA and UK you'll see a Google-certified consent form. You can change your
      ad choices at any time in <strong>Settings → Ad privacy choices</strong>.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Security and storage</h2>
    <p>
      All traffic between the app and our servers is encrypted with <strong>HTTPS (TLS)</strong>. Account data is
      stored in MongoDB Atlas, encrypted at rest and in transit.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Your rights and deleting your data</h2>
    <p>
      Your data belongs to you. You can delete your account and all of its watch history at any time in the app under
      <strong>Settings → Delete account</strong>{site.supportEmail && ', or by emailing us'}. Deletion is permanent.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Children</h2>
    <p>Zenith is not directed at children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect their personal information.</p>

    <h2>7. Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about this policy?
      {
        site.supportEmail ? (
          <>
            Email <a href={`mailto:${site.supportEmail}`}>{site.supportEmail}</a>.
          </>
        ) : (
          <>
            See the <a href="/support">support page</a>.
          </>
        )
      }
    </p>
  </Prose>
</Base>
